---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Ali Alhejab is an AI engineer based in Saudi Arabia, working on generative imaging, diffusion models, inference optimization, knowledge distillation, and Arabic ASR/NLP."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="shell page-header-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="page-kicker eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">AI engineer, focused on the gap between research and production.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="page-lede">
        Four years of hands-on ML, NLP, and LLM engineering. A bias toward measurement, clear
        baselines, and systems that can be explained.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="about-shell">
    <div class="shell about-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="about-intro">
          I'm <strong>Ali Alhejab</strong>, an AI engineer based in {SITE.location}. I work on generative
          imaging, diffusion models, inference optimization, knowledge distillation, and Arabic
          ASR/NLP.
        </p>

        <div class="about-copy">
          <p>
            My day-to-day work is about making models faster, smaller, or more useful without losing
            sight of the metric that matters. That often means building a reliable baseline first,
            then measuring where latency, cost, or quality actually goes. I've deployed models on
            NVIDIA H100 and B300 (Blackwell Ultra) hardware, which has made those trade-offs very
            concrete.
          </p>

          <h2>Background</h2>
          <p>
            I completed my MSc at King Abdullah University of Science and Technology (KAUST) and
            hold an NVIDIA certification. My research has been published with IEEE and Springer. I
            still think of publishing as an engineering exercise: define the claim, control the
            comparison, and report the result honestly.
          </p>

          <h2>What I write about</h2>
          <p>
            This site is where I keep longer notes on experiments, benchmarks, and engineering
            decisions. The posts lean practical: what I tried, what the numbers looked like, and
            what I would change next time. Some of it is about Arabic speech and language systems,
            where real-world audio and dialect variation tend to break tidy assumptions.
          </p>

          <h2>How I work</h2>
          <p>
            I prefer small, testable steps over large unverified jumps. In practice that means
            reproducible scripts, a clear evaluation set, and a healthy suspicion of a single
            benchmark. If a technique cannot be measured, it is hard to defend.
          </p>

          <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
          <p>
            You can find me on <a class="text-link" href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>,{' '}
            <a class="text-link" href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>, and{' '}
            <a class="text-link" href={SITE.huggingface}>Hugging Face</a>, or reach me by{' '}
            <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>email</a>. I also keep my{' '}
            <a class="text-link" href={SITE.scholar}>Google Scholar</a> profile up to date.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="about-side" aria-label="Background at a glance">
        <p class="about-side-head">At a glance</p>
        <dl class="about-facts">
          <div class="about-fact">
            <dt>Role</dt>
            <dd>{SITE.role}</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="about-fact">
            <dt>Experience</dt>
            <dd>~4 years hands-on ML / NLP / LLM</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="about-fact">
            <dt>Education</dt>
            <dd>MSc, KAUST</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="about-fact">
            <dt>Certification</dt>
            <dd>NVIDIA certified</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="about-fact">
            <dt>Research</dt>
            <dd>IEEE and Springer publications</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="about-fact">
            <dt>Hardware</dt>
            <dd>NVIDIA H100 and B300 (Blackwell Ultra)</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="about-fact">
            <dt>Location</dt>
            <dd>{SITE.location}</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <div class="about-side-foot">
          <a class="button button-ghost" href="/contact/">Get in touch <Icon name="arrow-right" size={15} /></a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
